      "title": "Auction sheet decoded: what R, A and 4.5 really mean",
      "excerpt": "Every mark on a Japanese auction sheet explained simply — so you bid with confidence.",
      "body": "A Japanese auction sheet is a condition report written in a shorthand of its own. Grades run from S (near-new) down through 4.5, 4.0, 3.5. Subjective marks like A (minor wear), B (scratches) and the dreaded R (repair history) appear next to each panel.\n\nAR7 translates every sheet into plain English and flags anything our inspection team wants verified by photo before you bid.\n\nRule of thumb: for export, aim for grade 4.0+, no R marks on structure, and always ask for underbody photos on diesel 4WD models."
    },
